  "question": {
    "text": "From a solid sphere of mass <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> and radius <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> a spherical portion of radius <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is removed, as shown in the figure. Taking gravitational potential <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the potential at the centre of the cavity thus formed is:<br />\r<br />\r<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>=Universal </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/P_45_Ques.jpg\" style=\"width: 196px; height: 189px;\" />\r<p>&nbsp;</p>\r",
